    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] adjust molar ratio of starting materials in CdCl2-HTAZ synthesis → changing reactant molar ratio directs assembly into different structures, including a 3D framework (3) versus a 1D chain (4)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] change one or more external stimuli such as solvent, temperature, counterions, pH, or molar ratio during MOF synthesis → controlled synthesis through external-stimulus variation provides a facile way to construct novel MOFs with unique structures and physical properties"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "complex 2 vs complex 3: winner=subject_a on thermal_stability"
    }
